content:
Evidence from the datasheet: **ordering** defines two SKUs (temperature grade only); **Recommended Operating Conditions** give one data-rate span (0.1–1.25 Gbps, typical 1.25); **Optical** gives TX λ max 1360 nm and RX λ max 1610 nm on the same module, not separate selectable modes. Per your rules, only the two part numbers are separate modes; bit rate **1.25** matches ordering; **1360** is the transmitter centre-wavelength maximum shared by both SKUs (RX **1610** is a different parameter on the same configuration, not a second mode).

```json
{
  "modes": [
    {
      "label": "LS-SM311G-20C Commercial 1.25G",
      "model": "LS-SM311G-20C",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1360.0,
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.25
    },
    {
      "label": "LS-SM311G-20I Industrial 1.25G",
      "model": "LS-SM311G-20I",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1360.0,
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.25
    }
  ]
}
```
